{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-130497" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6\\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}],$ find $det(C).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130497" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =det[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot det[\\begin{aligned}6\\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(8-18)\\cdot (36-10) \\\\  & =(-10)\\cdot 26 \\\\  & =-260.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130497" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57e4a8a42f490e6420b81cc38189dd5b3f8dc1be4d7da37908a7c1e3f18dcad0"} {"question" "q-130497" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130497" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-224"] ["math" "-236"] ["math" "-260"] ["math" "206"] ["math" "240"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130497" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-260"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-88266" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $B=[\\begin{aligned}6\\sqrt{2} & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}],$ find $det(B).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-88266" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =det[\\begin{aligned}6\\sqrt{2} & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot det[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(24-(-5))\\cdot (-14-(-12)) \\\\  & =29\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-58.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-88266" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57e4a8a42f490e6420b81cc38189dd5b3f8dc1be4d7da37908a7c1e3f18dcad0"} {"question" "q-88266" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-88266" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-158"] ["math" "-58"] ["math" "48"] ["math" "754"] ["math" "98"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-88266" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-58"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130493" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 7 \\\\ 4 & 8\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{aligned}],$ find $det(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130493" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 7 \\\\ 4 & 8\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot det[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(40-28)\\cdot (6-24) \\\\  & =12\\cdot (-18) \\\\  & =-216.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130493" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57e4a8a42f490e6420b81cc38189dd5b3f8dc1be4d7da37908a7c1e3f18dcad0"} {"question" "q-130493" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130493" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-120"] ["math" "-214"] ["math" "-216"] ["math" "126"] ["math" "206"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130493" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-216"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $Q=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 9 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],$ find $det(Q).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\ndet(Q)=det[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 9 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot det[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that both matrices are triangular. Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =(4\\cdot 5\\cdot (-1))\\cdot (3\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =(-20)\\cdot (-12) \\\\  & =240.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57e4a8a42f490e6420b81cc38189dd5b3f8dc1be4d7da37908a7c1e3f18dcad0"} {"question" "q-130484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-120"] ["math" "-224"] ["math" "204"] ["math" "220"] ["math" "240"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "240"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $P=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}8 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],$ find $det(P).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\ndet(P)=det[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot det[\\begin{aligned}8 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that both matrices are triangular. Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =(3\\cdot 1\\cdot (-2))\\cdot (8\\cdot 1\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =(-6)\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57e4a8a42f490e6420b81cc38189dd5b3f8dc1be4d7da37908a7c1e3f18dcad0"} {"question" "q-130488" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130488" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-24"] ["math" "-46"] ["math" "42"] ["math" "44"] ["math" "48"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130488" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "48"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-43063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $det({A}^{-1}),$ if $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-43063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $det(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =12+3 \\\\  & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}=\\frac{1}{15}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-43063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57e4a8a42f490e6420b81cc38189dd5b3f8dc1be4d7da37908a7c1e3f18dcad0"} {"question" "q-43063" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-43063" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{14}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{15}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{18}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{25}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{27}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-43063" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{15}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-43096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $det({A}^{-1}),$ if $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-43096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $det(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-12-9 \\\\  & =-21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}=-\\frac{1}{21}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-43096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57e4a8a42f490e6420b81cc38189dd5b3f8dc1be4d7da37908a7c1e3f18dcad0"} {"question" "q-43096" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-43096" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{21}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{7}"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{7}"] ["math" "-\\frac{7}{3}"] ["math" "21"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-43096" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{21}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130629" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $|{A}^{-1}|,$ if $A=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130629" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n|{A}^{-1}|=\\frac{1}{|A|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $|A|$ using a Laplace expansion across the $3$rd row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (-1)^{3+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (3+20) \\\\  & =-46\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n|{A}^{-1}|=\\frac{1}{|A|}=-\\frac{1}{46}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130629" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57e4a8a42f490e6420b81cc38189dd5b3f8dc1be4d7da37908a7c1e3f18dcad0"} {"question" "q-130629" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130629" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{36}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{44}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{46}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{23}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{42}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130629" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{46}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $|{A}^{-1}|,$ if $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n|{A}^{-1}|=\\frac{1}{|A|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $|A|$ using a Laplace expansion across the $2$nd column:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+1(-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+(-1)(-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2(-12+2)+(9-5)+(-6+20) \\\\  & =20+4+14 \\\\  & =38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n|{A}^{-1}|=\\frac{1}{|A|}=\\frac{1}{38}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57e4a8a42f490e6420b81cc38189dd5b3f8dc1be4d7da37908a7c1e3f18dcad0"} {"question" "q-130529" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130529" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{24}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{32}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{28}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{36}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{38}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130529" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{38}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-42584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $|{A}^{-1}|,$ if $A=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-42584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n|{A}^{-1}|=\\frac{1}{|A|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $|A|$ using a Laplace expansion across the $2$nd column:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{aligned}|+1(-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{aligned}|-2(-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(12-12)+(-15+24)+2(10-16) \\\\  & =0+9-12 \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n|{A}^{-1}|=\\frac{1}{|A|}=-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-42584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57e4a8a42f490e6420b81cc38189dd5b3f8dc1be4d7da37908a7c1e3f18dcad0"} {"question" "q-42584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-42584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{45}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{75}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{21}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{37}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-42584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-88298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n$|\\begin{aligned}a+2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ b+3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ c & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|=5,$\nfind \n$|\\begin{aligned}a+1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ b & 4 & 2 \\\\ c & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-88298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We \"factor out\" the given determinant from the determinant we would like to find:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}a+1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ b & 4 & 2 \\\\ c & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}(a+2)-1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ (b+3)-3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ c+0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNow, using the linearity property of determinants and expanding the second determinant across the $3$rd row, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}(a+2)-1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ (b+3)-3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ c+0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & ={{|\\begin{aligned}(a+2) & -2 & 2 \\\\ (b+3) & 4 & 2 \\\\ c & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|}_{⏟}}_{5}+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5+1\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5+(-10) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-88298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57e4a8a42f490e6420b81cc38189dd5b3f8dc1be4d7da37908a7c1e3f18dcad0"} {"question" "q-88298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-88298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-88298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130634" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$|\\begin{aligned}160 & 184 & 76 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 160 & 184 & 78\\end{aligned}|=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130634" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the $1$st row of our determinant is almost equal to the $3$rd row. So, we can rewrite the given determinant, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}160 & 184 & 76 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 160 & 184 & 78\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}160 & 184 & 76 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 160+0 & 184+0 & 76+2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using the linearity property of determinants, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}160 & 184 & 76 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 160+0 & 184+0 & 76+2\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}160 & 184 & 76 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 160 & 184 & 76\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}160 & 184 & 76 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first determinant must be zero since it has two identical rows, while the second determinant can be expanded across the $3$rd row, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}160 & 184 & 76 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 160 & 184 & 76\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}160 & 184 & 76 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =0+2(-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}160 & 184 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (160\\cdot 4-184\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 88 \\\\  & =176\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130634" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57e4a8a42f490e6420b81cc38189dd5b3f8dc1be4d7da37908a7c1e3f18dcad0"} {"question" "q-130634" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130634" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "154"] ["math" "168"] ["math" "172"] ["math" "176"] ["math" "88"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130634" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "176"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-42581" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n$|\\begin{aligned}a+3 & -5 \\\\ b & 6\\end{aligned}|=-7$,\nfind \n$|\\begin{aligned}a+2 & -5 \\\\ b+4 & 6\\end{aligned}|.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-42581" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We \"factor out\" the given determinant from the determinant we would like to find:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}a+2 & -5 \\\\ b+4 & 6\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}(a+3)-1 & -5 \\\\ b+4 & 6\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the linearity property of determinants, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}(a+3)-1 & -5 \\\\ b+4 & 6\\end{aligned}| & ={{|\\begin{aligned}a+3 & -5 \\\\ b & 6\\end{aligned}|}_{⏟}}_{-7}+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-7+(-6+20) \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-42581" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57e4a8a42f490e6420b81cc38189dd5b3f8dc1be4d7da37908a7c1e3f18dcad0"} {"question" "q-42581" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-42581" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-11"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "13"] ["math" "21"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-42581" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130777" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n$|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ a & b+2\\end{aligned}|=8$,\nfind \n$|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ a+3 & b\\end{aligned}|.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130777" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We \"factor out\" the given determinant from the determinant we would like to find:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ a+3 & b\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ a+3 & (b+2)-2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the linearity property of determinants, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ a+3 & (b+2)-2\\end{aligned}| & ={{|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ a & b+2\\end{aligned}|}_{⏟}}_{8}+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =8+(-6+6) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130777" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57e4a8a42f490e6420b81cc38189dd5b3f8dc1be4d7da37908a7c1e3f18dcad0"} {"question" "q-130777" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130777" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-14"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-130777" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-88296" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n$|\\begin{aligned}a & b & c \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|=4,$\nfind \n$|\\begin{aligned}a+1 & b & c \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-88296" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We \"factor out\" the given determinant from the determinant we would like to find:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}a+1 & b & c \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}a+1 & b+0 & c+0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the linearity property of determinants and expanding the second determinant across the $1$st row, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}a+1 & b+0 & c+0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & ={{|\\begin{aligned}a & b & c \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|}_{⏟}}_{4}+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4+1(-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4+1 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/state.json" "file_sha256" "6113454b0fdad32e630c0212515be363ff2965d77bd69703057b3d19f1d7dc9a"} {"question" "q-88296" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57e4a8a42f490e6420b81cc3818